   "widgets_values": [
    "High-resolution architectural visualization. \npreserve geometry, the building volume, identical roofline and slopes, precise original window layout and door frame cutouts, exact building proportions and structural massing from image 1\nExtremely strict adherence to the reference image geometry from image 1: exact replica of the building volume, identical roofline and slopes, precise original window layout and door frame cutouts, exact building proportions and structural massing. Apply modern facade finishing materials while keeping the architectural layout and silhouette 100% identical to the source structure, photorealistic render, crisp architectural lines, physically correct geometry.\n\nfacing brick masonry cladding, pale ash-grey brick, warm light beige brick tones, running bond pattern, horizontal brick coursing, thin flush mortar joints, matte chalky brick texture, subtle surface imperfections, smooth painted fibre-cement render, charcoal graphite smooth walls, seamless flush joints, matte monolithic finish, vertical wood slat cladding, narrow vertical larch planks, warm natural wood tones, amber honey wood, smooth planed wood texture, visible wood grain, vertical rhythm, narrow shadow gaps, soft matte surfaces, no gloss, soft daylight, subtle joint shadows, architectural material study, high-resolution facade texture, PBR materials, physically accurate textures, photorealistic architectural visualization, detailed surface finish\n\nphotorealistic, 8k resolution, professional architectural photography, soft natural daylight, sharp focus.",
    1536,
    "blurry, low quality, low resolution, jpeg artifacts, pixelated, out of focus, soft edges, hazy, construction waste, building materials, scaffolding, stacked bricks, bags of cement, dirt heaps, mud, trenches, excavator, construction machinery, gravel piles, unfinished ground, construction debris, trash, tools, changed building structure, altered proportions, modified roofline, added extra floors, shifted walls, deformed architecture, plastic render, drawing, distorted geometry."
